            "id": "44427536-62ca-34f4-b43b-e1416a9d16ce",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "What crypto investors need to know about the wash-sale rule",
            "description": "<p>Charles Schwab <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.schwab.com/learn/story/primer-on-wash-sales\">defines</a> a wash sale as \"when you sell a security at a loss for the tax benefits but then turn around and buy the same or a similar security.\" The IRS has rules about wash sales, but, at the end of 2025, these rules don't apply to cryptocurrencies (but they may apply to crypto exchange-traded products).</p>\n<p>Claris Financial Advisors founder Lee Baker shares what crypto investors need to know about the wash-sale rule.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination-overtime/\">Market Domination Overtime</a>.</p>",
